  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5425",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with SW837 through multiple pathways, all involving the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound acts as a target of doxorubicin, which in turn targets P2X purinoceptor 1 or GDM-1, both of which are ultimately directed to SW837. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin exerts its effect via a mechanism that involves the inhibition of P2X purinoceptors or the binding of a related compound, which then modulates SW837. The final_score of 0.5865 across the three paths indicates a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains partially inferred. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on SW837 supports a unified pathway, though the precise biological mechanism linking doxorubicin to these targets and their subsequent impact on SW837 requires further investigation.",
